#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059528 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "64d7a092-1997-5305-b44c-47c41bc9ac57" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing Two Complex Numbers"}] :question/id #uuid "8369943c-d7d8-5b77-949b-b48a4a4a96d1" :question/math-academy-id "e-5780" :question/problem "Express $\\dfrac {4 + \\textrm{i}} {1 - \\textrm{i}}$ in the form $a+\\textrm{i}b$." :question/worked-solution "The denominator is $1-\\textrm{i}$ and its conjugate is $1+\\textrm{i}$. We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $1+\\textrm{i}$, so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\dfrac {4 + \\textrm{i}} {1 - \\textrm{i}} &=\\dfrac {4 + \\textrm{i}} {1 - \\textrm{i}} \\cdot \\dfrac {1 + \\textrm{i}} {1 + \\textrm{i}} \\\\[5pt] &= \\dfrac {4 + 4\\textrm{i} + \\textrm{i} + \\textrm{i}^2} {1^2 - \\textrm{i}^2} \\\\[5pt] &= \\dfrac {4 + 5\\textrm{i} + (-1)} {1 - (-1)} \\\\[5pt] &= \\dfrac {3 + 5\\textrm{i}} {2} \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+\\textrm{i} b$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\dfrac {3 + 5\\textrm{i}} {2} = \\dfrac{3} {2} + \\dfrac {5} {2} \\textrm{i} \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059529 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "730fc9a7-a1b8-55a4-b8d3-666f87b82958" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Complex Number by an Imaginary Number"}] :question/id #uuid "107d76c0-349a-549d-adeb-f009492cd79c" :question/math-academy-id "e-5781" :question/problem "If $z_1 = -8-3\\textrm{i}$ and $z_2 = 2\\textrm{i}$, then what is $z_1$ divided by $z_2$?" :question/worked-solution "First, we set up the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {-8 - 3\\textrm{i}} {2\\textrm{i}}\n$$\n\nThe denominator is the imaginary number $2\\textrm{i}$. Note that this can be written as $0+2\\textrm{i}$, so the conjugate is $0-2\\textrm{i}$, or simply $-2\\textrm{i}$.\n\nSo, we multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-2\\textrm{i}$, so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\dfrac {-8 - 3\\textrm{i}} {2\\textrm{i}} &= \\dfrac {-8 - 3\\textrm{i}} {2\\textrm{i}} \\cdot \\dfrac {-2\\textrm{i}} {-2\\textrm{i}} \\\\[5pt] &= \\dfrac {16\\textrm{i} + 6\\textrm{i}^2} {-4\\textrm{i}^2} \\\\[5pt] &= \\dfrac {16\\textrm{i} + 6(-1)} {-4(-1)} \\\\[5pt] &= \\dfrac {-6 + 16\\textrm{i}} {4} \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b \\textrm{i}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\dfrac {-6 + 16\\textrm{i}} {4} &=-\\dfrac{6}{4} + \\dfrac{16}{4} \\textrm{i} \\\\[5pt] &= -\\dfrac{3} {2} + 4\\textrm{i} \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059530 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "27da4eb7-48c8-58f4-9676-c88d659f5fbb" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing an Imaginary Number by a Complex Number"}] :question/id #uuid "74740363-2309-5680-9373-05ce0fed9bcf" :question/math-academy-id "e-6230" :question/problem "If $z_1=3\\textrm{i}$ and $z_2 = 2+5\\textrm{i}$, then what is $z_1$ divided by $z_2$?" :question/worked-solution "First, we set up the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3\\textrm{i}}{2+5\\textrm i}\n$$\n\nThe denominator is $2+5\\textrm{i}$ and its conjugate is $2-5\\textrm{i}$. We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $2-5\\textrm{i}$, so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\dfrac {3 \\textrm{i}} {2 +5\\textrm{i}} &= \\dfrac {3 \\textrm{i}} {2 +5 \\textrm{i}} \\cdot \\dfrac {2 -5 \\textrm{i}} {2-5\\textrm{i}} \\\\[5pt] &=\\dfrac {6 \\textrm{i} - 15 \\textrm{i}^2} {2^2 - (5\\textrm{i})^2} \\\\[5pt] &=\\dfrac {6 \\textrm{i} - 15\\textrm{i}^2} {4 - 25\\textrm{i}^2} \\\\[5pt] &= \\dfrac {6 \\textrm{i} - 15(-1)} {4 - 25(-1)} \\\\[5pt] &=\\dfrac {6 \\textrm{i} + 15} {29} \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b \\textrm{i}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\dfrac {6 \\textrm{i} + 15} {29}= \\dfrac{15} {29} + \\dfrac {6} {29} \\textrm{i} \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059531 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "678ba6cb-b259-5a25-858c-9db161a34ca9" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Real Number by a Complex Number"}] :question/id #uuid "2fc036dd-7732-50ed-adef-8c37bd87fecd" :question/math-academy-id "e-6231" :question/problem "Express $\\dfrac{4}{-1+2\\textrm{i}}$ in the form $a+\\textrm{i}b$." :question/worked-solution "The denominator is $-1+2\\textrm{i}$ and its conjugate is $-1-2\\textrm{i}$. We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-1-2\\textrm{i}$, so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\dfrac {4} {-1 +2\\textrm{i}} &=\\dfrac {4} {-1 +2 \\textrm{i}} \\cdot \\dfrac {-1 -2 \\textrm{i}} {-1-2\\textrm{i}} \\\\[5pt] &= \\dfrac {-4 - 8 \\textrm{i}} {(-1)^2 - (2\\textrm{i})^2} \\\\[5pt] &= \\dfrac {-4 - 8 \\textrm{i}} {1 - 4\\textrm{i}^2} \\\\[5pt] &= \\dfrac {-4 - 8 \\textrm{i}} {1 - 4(-1)} \\\\[5pt] &= \\dfrac {-4 - 8 \\textrm{i}} {5} \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b \\textrm{i}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\dfrac {-4 - 8 \\textrm{i}} {5} = -\\dfrac{4} {5} - \\dfrac {8} {5} \\textrm{i} \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275628 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "27da4eb7-48c8-58f4-9676-c88d659f5fbb" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing an Imaginary Number by a Complex Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1de0b10b-47fe-56b5-b937-b5569e5e9101" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275630}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1de0b10b-47fe-56b5-b937-b5569e5e9101" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275630} :answer-field/id #uuid "764ff62d-2f8e-5ef3-af41-de7e5875e934" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275629} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c0eb84b-6c92-5b7e-a069-18784297930a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275632}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2c0eb84b-6c92-5b7e-a069-18784297930a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275632} :answer-field/id #uuid "c07b9bab-4835-5fbd-a748-3f03e4df9125" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275631}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e8165711-54b7-5043-aeb6-860843b30537" :question/math-academy-id "q-316847" :question/problem "Evaluate the expression below, expressing your answer in the form $a+b\\text{i},$ where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers.\n\n$\\frac{5\\text{i}}{1+3\\text{i}}=($\n{{field-1}} \n$)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\,\\text{i}$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator is $1+3\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $1-3\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $1-3\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5\\text{i}}{1+3\\text{i}} & =\\frac{5\\text{i}}{1+3\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{1-3\\text{i}}{1-3\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\text{i}-15{\\text{i}}^{2}}{{1}^{2}-(3\\text{i})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\text{i}-15(-1)}{1-(-9)} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\text{i}+15}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{15+5\\text{i}}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{15+5\\text{i}}{10}=(\\frac{3}{2})+(\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\text{i}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265137 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "27da4eb7-48c8-58f4-9676-c88d659f5fbb" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing an Imaginary Number by a Complex Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc6c30d1-8ecf-50e6-a66a-0909c2b8f0ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265139}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fc6c30d1-8ecf-50e6-a66a-0909c2b8f0ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265139} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c6ada72-28bf-5950-a297-c0f517d035b1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265138} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f5fc1cf-968d-5714-a780-e00c0a91b6cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{21}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265141}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0f5fc1cf-968d-5714-a780-e00c0a91b6cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{21}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265141} :answer-field/id #uuid "86bdf9c3-c1fb-5167-946d-240bbabbd436" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265140}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e535981f-647e-56d4-8c1b-fdc761659fc0" :question/math-academy-id "q-316848" :question/problem "Evaluate the expression below, expressing your answer in the form $a+b\\text{i},$ where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers.\n\n$\\frac{7\\text{i}}{3-\\text{i}}=($\n{{field-1}} \n$)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\,\\text{i}$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator is $3-\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $3+\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $3+\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7\\text{i}}{3-\\text{i}} & =\\frac{7\\text{i}}{3-\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{3+\\text{i}}{3+\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{21\\text{i}+7{\\text{i}}^{2}}{{3}^{2}-(\\text{i})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{21\\text{i}+7(-1)}{9-(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-7+21\\text{i}}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{-7+21\\text{i}}{10}=(-\\frac{7}{10})+(\\frac{21}{10})\\,\\text{i}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265179 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "64d7a092-1997-5305-b44c-47c41bc9ac57" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing Two Complex Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c37ba39-e719-5983-9ff5-f6447f7e974e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{16}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265181} {:answer/id #uuid "69274d97-1df3-54e5-a65e-c988603ba447" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265182}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c37ba39-e719-5983-9ff5-f6447f7e974e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{16}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265181} :answer-field/id #uuid "095e16a8-3a79-5cc1-b77c-c18462414596" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265180} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9bdc5b66-6608-56d4-bd89-df374350f4a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265184}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9bdc5b66-6608-56d4-bd89-df374350f4a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265184} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed86f562-7f92-581c-8aba-9ee39c907bd9" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265183}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1599423c-9248-5ffa-9d17-823c2bf2328f" :question/math-academy-id "q-316904" :question/problem "Evaluate the expression below, expressing your answer in the form $a+b\\text{i},$ where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers.\n\n$\\frac{5+2\\text{i}}{-2-3\\text{i}}=($\n{{field-1}} \n$)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\,\\text{i}$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator is $-2-3\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $-2+3\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-2+3\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5+2\\text{i}}{-2-3\\text{i}} & =\\frac{5+2\\text{i}}{-2-3\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{-2+3\\text{i}}{-2+3\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(5+2\\text{i})(-2+3\\text{i})}{(-2)^{2}-(3\\text{i})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-10+15\\text{i}-4\\text{i}+6{\\text{i}}^{2}}{4-(-9)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-10+11\\text{i}+6(-1)}{13} \\\\  & =\\frac{-16+11\\text{i}}{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-16+11\\text{i}}{13}=(-\\frac{16}{13})+(\\frac{11}{13})\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265206 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "678ba6cb-b259-5a25-858c-9db161a34ca9" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Real Number by a Complex Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bea7014a-2ec7-5bc1-9286-c1ed2aadf3c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{18}{13}-\\frac{27}{13}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265208} {:answer/id #uuid "917b6f05-edd5-53dc-8a8e-3a94bc2e3f1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{27}{13}+\\frac{18}{13}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265209} {:answer/id #uuid "25ea1f31-37a2-55c3-8cca-9c788a9e0c4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{27}{13}+\\frac{18}{13}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265210} {:answer/id #uuid "25e30022-e454-5b13-933e-a1a0a68b584c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{27}{13}-\\frac{18}{13}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265211} {:answer/id #uuid "50a4f5be-7f4f-5da6-b15b-e24fe8e99cf9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{27}{13}-\\frac{18}{13}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265212}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "50a4f5be-7f4f-5da6-b15b-e24fe8e99cf9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{27}{13}-\\frac{18}{13}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265212} :answer-field/id #uuid "bfdf262a-8a69-5f89-9cb7-40b82cfbac0d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265207}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3ca3346d-d2b9-53ea-9f84-d9305b392ee5" :question/math-academy-id "q-74648" :question/problem "$\\frac{9}{-3+2\\text{i}}=$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator is $-3+2\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $-3-2\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-3-2\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9}{-3+2\\text{i}} & =\\frac{9}{-3+2\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{-3-2\\text{i}}{-3-2\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-27-18\\text{i}}{9+6\\text{i}-6\\text{i}-4{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-27-18\\text{i}}{9-4(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-27-18\\text{i}}{9+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{-27-18\\text{i}}{13}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-27-18\\text{i}}{13}=-\\frac{27}{13}-\\frac{18}{13}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265213 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "730fc9a7-a1b8-55a4-b8d3-666f87b82958" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Complex Number by an Imaginary Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d3ae78aa-a8ba-5371-9a04-15acfd48b66f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2}-\\frac{3}{8}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265215} {:answer/id #uuid "15b6bed4-902c-5c4e-becf-c810855b2013" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}+\\frac{1}{8}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265216} {:answer/id #uuid "b3423c26-80ab-5b46-b4b5-59bfd96f259c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{1}{8}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265217} {:answer/id #uuid "c4eabb36-f6b3-577e-9d33-49b95f12f027" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}-\\frac{1}{8}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265218} {:answer/id #uuid "f147c615-f613-5bfb-ac8f-6df935875467" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{5}{8}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265219}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b3423c26-80ab-5b46-b4b5-59bfd96f259c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{1}{8}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265217} :answer-field/id #uuid "e48681cf-2d37-5061-9ef2-e8325e724d7d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265214}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6b1df748-6885-5736-937a-15d2623e818b" :question/math-academy-id "q-74659" :question/problem "If ${z}_{1}=1-12\\text{i}$ and ${z}_{2}=8\\text{i}$, then ${z}_{1}$ divided by ${z}_{2}$ equals" :question/worked-solution "First, we set up the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1-12\\text{i}}{8\\text{i}}\n$$\n\nThe denominator is the imaginary number $8\\text{i}.$ Note that this can be written as $0+8\\text{i},$ so the conjugate is $0-8\\text{i},$ or simply $-8\\text{i}.$\n\nSo, we multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-8\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{z}_{1}}{{z}_{2}} & =\\frac{1-12\\text{i}}{8\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-12\\text{i}}{8\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{-8\\text{i}}{-8\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-8\\text{i}+96{\\text{i}}^{2}}{-64{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-8\\text{i}+96(-1)}{-64(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-96-8\\text{i}}{64}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-96-8\\text{i}}{64}=-\\frac{96}{64}-\\frac{8}{64}\\text{i}=-\\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{1}{8}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060370 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "27da4eb7-48c8-58f4-9676-c88d659f5fbb" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing an Imaginary Number by a Complex Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c9eba4f7-b1d0-50e9-be98-00ba1aea8352" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2} - \\frac{3}{2}\\textrm{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059204} {:answer/id #uuid "11f70417-93a3-55e4-a3be-2fa2e96d5c26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2} - \\frac{3}{2}\\textrm{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059205} {:answer/id #uuid "2884a1ba-ffba-56a3-8ab5-f970246b15dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 + 3\\textrm{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059206} {:answer/id #uuid "5ff0c628-d0de-5903-8999-0ab70f1fdaa4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2} + \\frac{3}{2}\\textrm{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059207} {:answer/id #uuid "7e229f67-6464-5089-af2f-0b2da0e6b904" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 - 3\\textrm{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059208}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ff0c628-d0de-5903-8999-0ab70f1fdaa4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2} + \\frac{3}{2}\\textrm{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059207} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf4dec5c-b82c-5c00-8bcf-aa31113066b2" :answer-field/ke